IPU_v2_001

Self-Service OS Upgrade Initiation
As an Application Team Engineer,
I want to be able to self-service trigger an OS upgrade for my EC2 instances without raising a manual request to the platform team,
So that I can upgrade my servers at a time that suits my application schedule and reduce dependency on third-party operational teams.

Scenario: Application team triggers an upgrade for a target instance

Given an application team engineer has access to the OS Upgrade as a Service platform

When they select a target EC2 instance and initiate an upgrade request

Then the platform must automatically begin the upgrade workflow without requiring manual intervention from the platform team

And the requesting engineer must receive confirmation that the upgrade has been initiated.

Scenario: Upgrade is rejected when the target instance does not meet pre-upgrade eligibility criteria

Given an application team engineer initiates an upgrade request

When the pre-upgrade eligibility checks run

Then any instance that does not meet the required criteria (e.g., not in approved scope, unsupported OS family) must be rejected with a clear reason

And no upgrade workflow must proceed for the rejected instance.




 

IPU_v2_002

Multi-Cloud Upgrade Coverage
As a Platform Engineer,
I want the OS upgrade service to operate consistently across both the BA and IAG AWS cloud environments,
So that application teams across both clouds can benefit from the same governed, automated upgrade capability without requiring separate tooling or manual processes per cloud.

Scenario: Upgrade is executed successfully in the BA cloud environment

Given a target EC2 instance exists in the BA cloud

When an upgrade is initiated

Then the platform must provision, configure, and validate the new instance within the BA cloud environment using the correct account, networking, and IAM configuration.

Scenario: Upgrade is executed successfully in the IAG cloud environment

Given a target EC2 instance exists in the IAG cloud

When an upgrade is initiated

Then the platform must provision, configure, and validate the new instance within the IAG cloud environment using the correct account, networking, and IAM configuration.

Scenario: Cloud boundary is enforced

Given an upgrade request targets an instance in one cloud

When the platform executes the upgrade workflow

Then all new resources must be created within the same cloud boundary as the source instance

And no cross-cloud resource movement must occur.




 

IPU_v2_003

IaC and Non-IaC Workload Support
As an Application Team Engineer,
I want the upgrade service to work regardless of whether my EC2 instance is managed by Infrastructure as Code or was provisioned manually,
So that both modern IaC-managed workloads and legacy manually-provisioned servers can be upgraded through the same service without requiring me to first introduce IaC.

Scenario: Upgrade succeeds for an IaC-managed instance

Given a target EC2 instance is managed by Terraform or another approved IaC tool

When an upgrade is initiated

Then the platform must use IaC state and manifests to inform the new instance configuration

And the upgrade must complete successfully without requiring the application team to manually reconstruct instance configuration.

Scenario: Upgrade succeeds for a non-IaC instance

Given a target EC2 instance was provisioned manually and has no associated IaC state

When an upgrade is initiated

Then the platform must discover the source instance configuration (tags, IAM instance profile, security groups, network settings) through the AWS API

And use this discovered configuration to provision the replacement instance

And the upgrade must complete successfully without requiring the application team to first write IaC.

Scenario: Discovery of instance configuration is auditable

Given an upgrade is performed for a non-IaC instance

When the platform reads the source instance configuration

Then all discovered configuration values used to provision the replacement must be recorded as part of the upgrade evidence record.




 

IPU_v2_004

RedHat and Windows Operating System Support
As a Platform Engineer,
I want the OS upgrade service to support both RedHat Enterprise Linux and Windows Server operating systems,
So that the widest possible range of application workloads can be upgraded through a single governed service regardless of their OS family.

Scenario: Upgrade succeeds for a RedHat Enterprise Linux instance

Given a target EC2 instance runs a supported version of RedHat Enterprise Linux (including RHEL 6)

When an upgrade is initiated

Then the platform must provision a replacement instance using the latest ECP-approved RHEL golden image

And apply all required BA policy and security controls for the RHEL OS family

And complete the upgrade workflow successfully.

Scenario: Upgrade succeeds for a Windows Server instance

Given a target EC2 instance runs a supported version of Windows Server

When an upgrade is initiated

Then the platform must provision a replacement instance using the latest ECP-approved Windows golden image

And apply all required BA policy and security controls for the Windows OS family

And complete the upgrade workflow successfully.

Scenario: Unsupported OS version is rejected at pre-check

Given a target EC2 instance runs an OS version that is not listed in the approved upgrade matrix

When the pre-upgrade eligibility check runs

Then the platform must reject the upgrade request with a clear message identifying the unsupported OS version

And no new instance must be provisioned.




 

IPU_v2_005

BA Policy and Standards Compliance via ECP Golden Image
As a Cyber Security Engineer,
I want every upgraded EC2 instance to start from the latest ECP-approved golden image so that it is fully compliant with all British Airways policies and security standards from the moment it is provisioned,
So that we eliminate the risk of configuration drift, inherited vulnerabilities, and policy gaps that exist on long-running servers.

Scenario: New instance is provisioned from the latest ECP golden image

Given an upgrade is initiated for any EC2 instance regardless of OS family

When the replacement instance is provisioned

Then the platform must use the latest version of the ECP-approved golden image for the target OS family as the base AMI

And the golden image version used must be recorded as part of the upgrade evidence record.

Scenario: Policy compliance is validated after provisioning

Given a replacement instance has been provisioned from the ECP golden image

When post-provisioning compliance checks run

Then all BA mandatory security controls and hardening requirements must be confirmed as present on the new instance

And any failed control must block the upgrade workflow and trigger a rollback or remediation.

Scenario: Golden image version is traceable across all upgrades

Given multiple upgrades are performed over time using different golden image versions

When compliance evidence is reviewed

Then each upgrade record must identify the exact golden image version used

And allow auditors to confirm that the approved ECP baseline was applied for every upgrade.




 

IPU_v2_006

Automated Upgrade Orchestration
As a Platform Engineer,
I want the upgrade process to be automated end-to-end — from pre-checks through provisioning, configuration, data copy, and post-upgrade validation — with minimal manual steps required from the application team,
So that the upgrade service can scale across a large number of instances without proportional operational effort and produce consistent, predictable outcomes every time.

Scenario: Pre-upgrade checks are performed automatically

Given an upgrade is initiated for a target EC2 instance

When the upgrade workflow starts

Then the platform must automatically run all required pre-upgrade eligibility and health checks (OS family, version eligibility, account health, available IP/quota, policy compliance) before any new resource is created

And the result of each pre-check must be recorded.

Scenario: Replacement instance is provisioned automatically

Given all pre-upgrade checks have passed

When the upgrade workflow proceeds to provisioning

Then the platform must automatically provision a new EC2 instance using the approved golden image, copying metadata, IAM instance profile, security groups, and network configuration from the source instance

And the application team must not be required to manually configure the replacement instance.

Scenario: Data and configuration are copied automatically

Given the replacement instance has been provisioned

When the data migration step runs

Then the platform must automatically create new storage volumes that mirror the source instance's attached volumes and copy all data across to the replacement instance

And the copy operation must be validated before the workflow proceeds.

Scenario: Post-upgrade validation is performed automatically

Given data and configuration have been copied to the replacement instance

When the validation step runs

Then the platform must automatically verify that the replacement instance is healthy, compliant with BA policies, and ready for the application team to test

And the validation result must be recorded as compliance evidence.




 

IPU_v2_007

Side-by-Side Upgrade Model — No Instance Introduction or Termination
As an Application Team Engineer,
I want the upgrade service to provision the new instance alongside the existing one — keeping both running at the same time — without the platform service introducing or terminating instances into or from my live stack,
So that I retain full control over when traffic is moved to the new server and when the old server is decommissioned, allowing me to validate the new environment at my own pace.

Scenario: Source instance remains running throughout the upgrade

Given an upgrade has been initiated for a target EC2 instance

When the platform provisions and configures the replacement instance

Then the source instance must continue running and be accessible throughout the entire upgrade process

And the platform must not stop, terminate, or modify the source instance.

Scenario: Replacement instance is delivered but not inserted into the live stack

Given the replacement instance is ready and validated

When the upgrade workflow completes its platform steps

Then the replacement instance must be available to the application team for testing

And the platform must not automatically redirect traffic, update load balancer target groups, or change any DNS or routing configuration

And the application team retains full control over when and how to introduce the replacement instance into their live environment.

Scenario: Platform does not terminate the source or replacement instance

Given the upgrade workflow has completed or encountered a failure

When the workflow reaches its final state

Then the platform must not terminate either the source instance or the replacement instance

And decommissioning of the source instance remains the sole responsibility of the application team.

Scenario: Blue-green testing window is supported

Given both source and replacement instances are running concurrently

When the application team performs validation testing on the replacement instance

Then both instances must remain available simultaneously for as long as the application team requires before they decide to commit to the change.




 

IPU_v2_008

Instance Metadata, IAM, Security Group, and Data Migration
As an Application Team Engineer,
I want the upgrade service to automatically replicate the source instance's metadata, IAM instance profile, security groups, and attached data to the replacement instance,
So that the replacement instance is as close to the source configuration as possible without requiring me to manually reconstruct settings or risk losing data.

Scenario: Instance metadata is copied to the replacement instance

Given a source EC2 instance has tags and metadata applied

When the replacement instance is provisioned

Then all tags and relevant metadata must be copied from the source instance to the replacement instance

And any platform-managed upgrade tags must be added to the replacement instance to identify it as a replacement.

Scenario: IAM instance profile is applied to the replacement instance

Given a source EC2 instance has an IAM instance profile attached

When the replacement instance is provisioned

Then the same IAM instance profile must be applied to the replacement instance

And the assignment must be validated as part of the provisioning step.

Scenario: Security groups are applied to the replacement instance

Given a source EC2 instance has one or more security groups attached

When the replacement instance is provisioned

Then the same security groups must be applied to the replacement instance

And the security group configuration must be validated before the workflow proceeds.

Scenario: Storage volumes are mirrored and data is copied to the replacement

Given a source EC2 instance has one or more attached EBS volumes

When the data migration step runs

Then new EBS volumes of equivalent type and size must be created for the replacement instance

And all data must be copied from the source volumes to the replacement volumes

And a checksum or equivalence validation must be performed to confirm data integrity before the workflow proceeds.




 

IPU_v2_009

Safe Rollback via Source Instance Retention
As an Application Team Engineer,
I want the source EC2 instance to remain fully intact and available throughout the upgrade process so that if the new instance does not work as expected I can immediately continue using the original,
So that the upgrade service provides a safe exit path that does not risk service availability for the application.

Scenario: Source instance is available for rollback at any point during the upgrade

Given an upgrade workflow is in progress or has completed

When the application team determines that the replacement instance does not meet their requirements

Then the application team must be able to immediately return to using the source instance

And the source instance must be in the same state as before the upgrade began (unchanged by the platform).

Scenario: No irreversible changes are made to the source instance

Given an upgrade workflow is running

When any step in the workflow executes

Then no step must modify, reconfigure, stop, or otherwise alter the source EC2 instance

And any changes required by the upgrade must be applied only to the replacement instance.

Scenario: Upgrade evidence records the rollback decision

Given an application team decides not to adopt the replacement instance and returns to the source

When the rollback decision is recorded

Then the platform must record the rollback outcome as part of the upgrade evidence

And the evidence must capture the reason, timestamp, and actor who initiated the rollback.




 

IPU_v2_010

Compliance Evidence and Auditability
As a Cyber Security Engineer,
I want every step of the OS upgrade process — pre-checks, provisioning, configuration, data migration, validation, and rollback — to produce tamper-evident, auditable compliance evidence,
So that the organisation can demonstrate that every upgraded instance was built from an approved golden image, is compliant with BA policies, and that the upgrade was performed in a controlled, governed manner.

Scenario: Evidence is produced for every upgrade workflow step

Given an upgrade workflow is executing

When each workflow step completes (pass or fail)

Then the platform must publish a compliance evidence record for that step

And the record must include the step name, outcome, timestamp, source instance identifier, replacement instance identifier, golden image version, and any relevant policy check results.

Scenario: Evidence is stored in a tamper-evident, immutable store

Given compliance evidence records are produced by the upgrade workflow

When each record is written

Then it must be stored in an immutable evidence store with write-once protection and cryptographic integrity controls

And the evidence must remain retrievable for the minimum required retention period.

Scenario: Audit trail covers all access and changes to evidence records

Given compliance evidence is stored

When an auditor or operator accesses or queries evidence records

Then a complete access and change audit trail must be maintained

And the trail must include who accessed the record, when, and what action was taken.

Scenario: Compliance evidence supports regulatory audit on demand

Given an auditor requests evidence of upgrade compliance for a specific instance or time period

When the report or evidence query is executed

Then the platform must be able to provide a complete, exportable record of all upgrade steps, policy check outcomes, golden image versions, and final instance state for the requested scope.
